## Current Rules

### foundations/

| Dewey | File | Always | Description |
|-------|------|--------|-------------|
| 001 | `stratified-design` | ✓ | Each layer a small language built on the one below; a one-way **DAG of abstraction** (SICP §2.2.4) — discovered per problem, not a fixed layer stack |
| 002 | `code-quality` | ✓ | Composable pipelines, no nested conditionals, DRY |
| 003 | `result-handling` | ✓ | success?/failed? predicates; schema constructors; factory functions for any repeated map shape (event envelopes, task records, etc.) |
| 004 | `validation-boundaries` | ✓ | Schemas at interface/external boundaries only |
| 005 | `exceptions-as-data` | ✓ | Anomalies as data in flows; throw only at absolute boundaries |
| 006 | `named-constants` | ✓ | No magic numbers / magic strings; every meaningful literal extracted to a `def` with an intent-bearing docstring |
| 007 | `config-as-data` | ✓ | Operational config lives in `.edn` files with a Malli schema; code holds only fallback defaults |
| 008 | `no-dead-code` | ✓ | Delete unused code in the change that obsoletes it; no commented-out blocks, no `_legacy` shims without an explicit removal plan |
| 009 | `self-documenting-code` | ✓ | Code is the artifact; comments explain WHY when non-obvious, never restate WHAT; self-document first; document the public boundary (interface), keep impl light (headers + docstrings exempt) |
| 010 | `simple-made-easy` | ✓ | Simplicity over familiarity, uncomplected artifacts |
| 011 | `layered-architecture` | ✓ | The Dependency Rule: module deps point inward only (Adapters→Application→Domain→Foundations); pure core; ports & adapters — one coarse module-level instance of 001 |
| 020 | `specification-standards` |  | Normative specs (N1-N6), spec governance, conformance |
| 021 | `work-spec-authoring` |  | `work/*.spec.edn` format: priority, theme, normative-refs, testable acceptance criteria |
| 030 | `runtime-no-host-docker-socket` | ✓ | Reject bind mounts of `/var/run/docker.sock` and equivalents (capsule isolation) |
| 031 | `runtime-require-rootless` | ✓ | Warn / hard-stop based on the runtime's `:rootless` capability |
| 032 | `runtime-restrict-host-mounts` | ✓ | Review host bind mounts outside an allowlist |
| 033 | `runtime-require-image-digest-pin` | ✓ | Reject execution plans whose `:image-digest` is not `sha256:<64-hex>` |
| 050 | `localization` | ✓ | No raw strings in any emitted output; user-facing → en-US.edn, system-facing → system.edn; msg/t lookup always |

### languages/

| Dewey | File | Always | Description |
|-------|------|--------|-------------|
| 210 | `clojure` | ✓ | Polylith + per-file stratified design, map access patterns |
| 211 | `clojure-exception-handling` | ✓ | Prefer slingshot `try+` / `throw+` (strict superset of `try`); plain `try` allowed in three narrow cases (no-slingshot-dep leaf catch, leaf inside `try+`, REPL/`(comment …)`) |
| 212 | `clojure-no-requiring-resolve` | clj/cljc | BLOCKING (`enforcement.action: hard-halt`): no `requiring-resolve` — use a direct `(:require …)`, fix load-order/design instead of lazy-resolving |
| 220 | `python` |  | Poetry, functional Python |
| 221 | `python-stratified-components` |  | Package = component: `interface.py` only surface, explicit-state functions, `@stratum(n)` monotonic ≤3 strata, flat leaves, DAG-among-impl-modules → extract component |
| 230 | `rust` |  | Workspaces, typed boundary commands, pipeline selection, data-driven content, toolchain (Rust 2024 + workspace lints), domain newtypes, dependency policy |
| 231 | `rust-async` |  | Don't block the runtime, no locks across `.await`, cancellation-aware `select!`, bounded channels, task lifecycle ownership, `Arc<Mutex<T>>` not as default architecture |
| 232 | `rust-unsafe` |  | `unsafe_code = "deny"` workspace-wide; isolated behind safe APIs; `// SAFETY:` comment on every site; performance alone insufficient |
| 233 | `rust-observability` |  | `tracing` not `println!`, correlation IDs via `#[instrument]`, error source-chain preservation, log strings localized to system locale |
| 234 | `rust-wire-protocols` |  | Wire structs separate from domain, versioned envelopes, validate-on-deserialize, append-only ratchet for audit-trail payloads |
| 235 | `rust-boundary-commands` |  | Typed command enums at boundary, exhaustive dispatch, pipeline selection by enum, bounded data-driven content, derived context at seams |
| 236 | `rust-stratified-modules` |  | `// ---- Layer N` headings (≥4 dashes) per file; fn calls strictly upward-from-caller (SL008), vocabulary refs ≤ own layer, types at minimal layer (SL009); ≤3 layers; thin index; stratum-lint-rs |
| 240 | `swift` |  | Swift conventions |
| 241 | `swift-stratified-files` |  | `// ---- Layer N` headings per file; func calls strictly upward-from-caller (SL008), vocabulary refs ≤ own layer, types at minimal layer (SL009); pure logic in top-level funcs, stateful shells delegate; stratum-lint-swift |
| 250 | `javascript` |  | Browser JS — sparse use, no globals, ES modules, no inline handlers, safe DOM |
| 260 | `css` |  | Design tokens, semantic class names, shallow selectors, accessible focus |
| 270 | `html` |  | Semantic elements, buttons-vs-links, labelled forms |

